                <pb facs="0287" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-31T13:00:00-06:00">January 31, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Referring to Department’s telegram of January 27, 3 p.m., circular. Under
                    Secretary Beteta says he feels sure Mexico is in agreement. I will see Minister
                    Hay tomorrow and report official approval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
